{"images":[],"manifest":{"budgetTokens":60000,"countMethod":"proxy","model":"gpt-6-luna","packSha":"4c0f07efc3c6269f3da59e9403a9add56a2d8cebfd255d2b2239baea021bfc4e","packTokens":9377,"recipeVersion":"1","redactions":0,"sections":[{"id":"tpl","tokens":315,"trimmed":false,"trust":"trusted"},{"id":"acs","tokens":6659,"trimmed":false,"trust":"derived"},{"id":"ac-tests","tokens":2346,"trimmed":false,"trust":"derived"},{"id":"task","tokens":18,"trimmed":false,"trust":"trusted"}],"stage":"author-tests"},"pointers":[],"system":"You check acceptance tests before they are locked. The code they test is not written yet, so every test fails today: do not judge whether a test passes.\nFor each criterion in \"acs\", open its tests (\"ac-tests\" gives the file and the test name; a criterion can have several, judge them together) and decide whether they prove the criterion.\n- \"proves-it\": code that broke any part of the criterion would fail these tests. They assert the values, messages, status codes and stored data the criterion names, for every case it names.\n- \"weak\": the tests could pass on code that does not meet the criterion. Typical: checking that some error exists instead of the one the criterion names, checking one case of several, not comparing a value the criterion says is unchanged, not setting up the starting state the criterion describes.\n- \"no-test\": nothing tests it.\nReport one verdict per criterion in \"coverage\", with testId \"\" unless one test is at fault. In \"why\", one sentence the test writer can act on: what is not asserted. Judge only against the criterion's own words; do not ask for more than it says.","tools":["read_file","search"],"toolsAt":"under-review","user":"<artifact id=\"acs\" kind=\"acceptance-criteria\" sha=\"\">\n[\n {\n  \"req\": \"REQ-1\",\n  \"given\": \"OAuth client ID and redirect URI are configured for deployment.\",\n  \"id\": \"AC-1.1\",\n  \"level\": \"api\",\n  \"then\": \"The response status is 200 and the response contains an `authorizationUrl` reflecting the configured client ID and redirect URI and a non-empty `state`.\",\n  \"when\": \"A client sends `GET /api/auth/google/authorization`.\"\n },\n {\n  \"req\": \"REQ-1\",\n  \"given\": \"Required Google OAuth configuration or authorization service is unavailable.\",\n  \"id\": \"AC-1.2\",\n  \"level\": \"api\",\n  \"then\": \"The response status is 503 and the response error contains the contract-defined `code`, `message`, and `field` values.\",\n  \"when\": \"A client sends `GET /api/auth/google/authorization`.\"\n },\n {\n  \"req\": \"REQ-2\",\n  \"given\": \"A valid Google Workspace authorization code and matching state identify an eligible Folio3 employee.\",\n  \"id\": \"AC-2.1\",\n  \"level\": \"api\",\n  \"then\": \"The response status is 200 and the response session contains `id`, `employeeId`, `employeeName`, `corporateEmail`, `role`, and `accessToken`.\",\n  \"when\": \"The client sends `POST /api/auth/sign-in` with `authorizationCode` and `state`.\"\n },\n {\n  \"req\": \"REQ-2\",\n  \"given\": \"OAuth values are configured and a valid authorization code is submitted.\",\n  \"id\": \"AC-2.2\",\n  \"level\": \"api\",\n  \"then\": \"The request sent to Google's token endpoint contains the configured client ID, client secret, redirect URI, authorization code, and state.\",\n  \"when\": \"The API exchanges the code with Google Workspace.\"\n },\n {\n  \"req\": \"REQ-2\",\n  \"given\": \"The sign-in request has a missing, invalid, or mismatched state or code, an ineligible identity, or Google service is unavailable.\",\n  \"id\": \"AC-2.3\",\n  \"level\": \"api\",\n  \"then\": \"The response status is 400 for an invalid request, 401 for an unaccepted identity, or 503 for an unavailable service, and each error response contains the contract-defined `code`, `message`, and `field` values.\",\n  \"when\": \"The client sends `POST /api/auth/sign-in`.\"\n },\n {\n  \"req\": \"REQ-3\",\n  \"given\": \"A valid bearer session identifies an employee with a profile and registered vehicles.\",\n  \"id\": \"AC-3.1\",\n  \"level\": \"api\",\n  \"then\": \"The response status is 200 and the response profile contains the contract's required employee fields, including `id`, `employeeId`, `employeeName`, `corporateEmail`, `dedicatedParking`, `assignedFloor`, `assignedSpace`, and the employee's `vehicles` list.\",\n  \"when\": \"The employee sends `GET /api/employees/me`.\"\n },\n {\n  \"req\": \"REQ-3\",\n  \"given\": \"The bearer token is absent or invalid, the identity lacks access, or no employee profile exists.\",\n  \"id\": \"AC-3.2\",\n  \"level\": \"api\",\n  \"then\": \"The response status is 401, 403, or 404 respectively, and the response error contains the contract-defined `code`, `message`, and `field` values.\",\n  \"when\": \"A client sends `GET /api/employees/me`.\"\n },\n {\n  \"req\": \"REQ-4\",\n  \"given\": \"A valid employee bearer session and available App database identify an employee.\",\n  \"id\": \"AC-4.1\",\n  \"level\": \"api\",\n  \"then\": \"The response status is 200 and the response dashboard contains the contract's required fields, including `officeDate`, `timezone`, `releaseTime`, `assignedSpace`, `spaceStatus`, `availableSpaces`, `registeredVehicle`, `workingDays`, and `workingDayRule`.\",\n  \"when\": \"The employee sends `GET /api/parking/dashboard`.\"\n },\n {\n  \"req\": \"REQ-4\",\n  \"given\": \"The request has no valid bearer token.\",\n  \"id\": \"AC-4.2\",\n  \"level\": \"api\",\n  \"then\": \"The response status is 401 and the response error contains the contract-defined `code`, `message`, and `field` values.\",\n  \"when\": \"A client sends `GET /api/parking/dashboard`.\"\n },\n {\n  \"req\": \"REQ-5\",\n  \"given\": \"The bearer session identifies an employee with dedicated parking and the submitted `officeDate` is today in the office timezone and releasable.\",\n  \"id\": \"AC-5.1\",\n  \"level\": \"api\",\n  \"then\": \"The response status is 200 and the response release contains `officeDate`, `space`, `status`, `claimableAt`, and `auditEvents`, including a `Released` action.\",\n  \"when\": \"The employee posts the today-release request.\"\n },\n {\n  \"req\": \"REQ-5\",\n  \"given\": \"The request is unauthenticated, the employee is not eligible to release dedicated parking, or the release conflicts with the current parking state.\",\n  \"id\": \"AC-5.2\",\n  \"level\": \"api\",\n  \"then\": \"The response status is 401, 403, or 409 respectively, and the response error contains the contract-defined `code`, `message`, and `field` values.\",\n  \"when\": \"A client posts to `/api/parking/releases/today`.\"\n },\n {\n  \"req\": \"REQ-6\",\n  \"given\": \"A valid employee bearer session identifies an employee with registered vehicles.\",\n  \"id\": \"AC-6.1\",\n  \"level\": \"api\",\n  \"then\": \"The response status is 200 and the response `vehicles` list contains only that employee's vehicles with contract fields, including `id`, `plate`, `make`, `model`, `color`, and `active`.\",\n  \"when\": \"The employee sends `GET /api/vehicles`.\"\n },\n {\n  \"req\": \"REQ-6\",\n  \"given\": \"The request has no valid bearer token.\",\n  \"id\": \"AC-6.2\",\n  \"level\": \"api\",\n  \"then\": \"The response status is 401 and the response error contains the contract-defined `code`, `message`, and `field` values.\",\n  \"when\": \"A client sends `GET /api/vehicles`.\"\n },\n {\n  \"req\": \"REQ-7\",\n  \"given\": \"A valid employee bearer session and vehicle input with a valid plate and optional make, model, and color are supplied.\",\n  \"id\": \"AC-7.1\",\n  \"level\": \"api\",\n  \"then\": \"The response status is 201 and the response vehicle record contains `id`, `plate`, `make`, `model`, `color`, and `active` set to true.\",\n  \"when\": \"The employee posts the vehicle input to `/api/vehicles`.\"\n },\n {\n  \"req\": \"REQ-7\",\n  \"given\": \"The vehicle input is invalid, the request is unauthenticated, or the plate conflicts with an existing record.\",\n  \"id\": \"AC-7.2\",\n  \"level\": \"api\",\n  \"then\": \"The response status is 400, 401, or 409 respectively, and the response error contains the contract-defined `code`, `message`, and `field` values.\",\n  \"when\": \"A client posts to `/api/vehicles`.\"\n },\n {\n  \"req\": \"REQ-8\",\n  \"given\": \"A valid employee bearer session identifies an employee with saved releases and audit events.\",\n  \"id\": \"AC-8.1\",\n  \"level\": \"api\",\n  \"then\": \"The response status is 200 and the response `releases` list contains only that employee's releases with contract fields, including `id`, `officeDate`, `space`, `status`, `claimableAt`, and `auditEvents`.\",\n  \"when\": \"The employee sends `GET /api/parking/releases`.\"\n },\n {\n  \"req\": \"REQ-8\",\n  \"given\": \"The request has no valid bearer token.\",\n  \"id\": \"AC-8.2\",\n  \"level\": \"api\",\n  \"then\": \"The response status is 401 and the response error contains the contract-defined `code`, `message`, and `field` values.\",\n  \"when\": \"A client sends `GET /api/parking/releases`.\"\n },\n {\n  \"req\": \"REQ-9\",\n  \"given\": \"A valid employee bearer session identifies a dedicated-parking holder and `officeDates` contains one or more valid dates within the next 30 calendar days.\",\n  \"id\": \"AC-9.1\",\n  \"level\": \"api\",\n  \"then\": \"The response status is 201 and the response `releases` list contains the saved dates and a `Scheduled` audit event for each release.\",\n  \"when\": \"The employee posts the schedule to `/api/parking/releases`.\"\n },\n {\n  \"req\": \"REQ-9\",\n  \"given\": \"The schedule request is malformed, the employee is not eligible, or dates violate the contract's date rules.\",\n  \"id\": \"AC-9.2\",\n  \"level\": \"api\",\n  \"then\": \"The response status is 400, 403, or 422 as applicable, and the response error contains the contract-defined `code`, `message`, and `field` values.\",\n  \"when\": \"A client posts to `/api/parking/releases`.\"\n },\n {\n  \"req\": \"REQ-10\",\n  \"given\": \"The bearer session owns an unclaimed scheduled release identified by `releaseId`.\",\n  \"id\": \"AC-10.1\",\n  \"level\": \"api\",\n  \"then\": \"The response status is 200, the response release status is `Cancelled`, and its `auditEvents` list includes scheduling and cancellation events.\",\n  \"when\": \"The employee deletes `/api/parking/releases/{releaseId}`.\"\n },\n {\n  \"req\": \"REQ-10\",\n  \"given\": \"The release does not exist, belongs to another employee, has already been claimed, or the request is unauthenticated.\",\n  \"id\": \"AC-10.2\",\n  \"level\": \"api\",\n  \"then\": \"The response status is 404, 403, 409, or 401 as applicable, and the response error contains the contract-defined `code`, `message`, and `field` values.\",\n  \"when\": \"A client deletes `/api/parking/releases/{releaseId}`.\"\n },\n {\n  \"req\": \"REQ-11\",\n  \"given\": \"A valid employee bearer session exists and office capacity, release time, and current parking allocations are configured.\",\n  \"id\": \"AC-11.1\",\n  \"level\": \"api\",\n  \"then\": \"The response status is 200 and the response contains `officeDate`, `timezone`, `availableSpaces`, `releaseTime`, and a `floors` list with `floor`, `freeSpaces`, and `totalSpaces`.\",\n  \"when\": \"The employee sends `GET /api/parking/availability`.\"\n },\n {\n  \"req\": \"REQ-11\",\n  \"given\": \"The request has no valid bearer token.\",\n  \"id\": \"AC-11.2\",\n  \"level\": \"api\",\n  \"then\": \"The response status is 401 and the response error contains the contract-defined `code`, `message`, and `field` values.\",\n  \"when\": \"A client sends `GET /api/parking/availability`.\"\n },\n {\n  \"req\": \"REQ-12\",\n  \"given\": \"A valid employee bearer session identifies an eligible employee, the selected registered vehicle belongs to that employee, and a space is claimable for `officeDate`.\",\n  \"id\": \"AC-12.1\",\n  \"level\": \"api\",\n  \"then\": \"The response status is 201 and the response contains allocated `floor`, `space`, `plate`, `officeDate`, `status`, `entryStatus`, `floorCapacity`, `allocationRule`, and `authorizationScope` fields.\",\n  \"when\": \"The employee posts `vehicleId` and `officeDate` to `/api/parking/claims`.\"\n },\n {\n  \"req\": \"REQ-12\",\n  \"given\": \"Two eligible employees attempt to claim the last available space for the same office date concurrently.\",\n  \"id\": \"AC-12.2\",\n  \"level\": \"api\",\n  \"then\": \"The responses contain exactly one status 201 and one conflict status 409, and the successful response contains one allocated space.\",\n  \"when\": \"The employees submit claims concurrently.\"\n },\n {\n  \"req\": \"REQ-12\",\n  \"given\": \"The request is invalid or unauthenticated, the employee is ineligible, the vehicle or date is not eligible, or no space remains available.\",\n  \"id\": \"AC-12.3\",\n  \"level\": \"api\",\n  \"then\": \"The response status is 400, 401, 403, 409, or 422 as applicable, and the response error contains the contract-defined `code`, `message`, and `field` values.\",\n  \"when\": \"A client posts to `/api/parking/claims`.\"\n },\n {\n  \"req\": \"REQ-13\",\n  \"given\": \"A valid employee bearer session identifies an employee with an active temporary allocation for today.\",\n  \"id\": \"AC-13.1\",\n  \"level\": \"api\",\n  \"then\": \"The response status is 200 and the response contains the allocation's required `ParkingClaim` fields, including `floor`, `space`, `plate`, `officeDate`, and `entryStatus`.\",\n  \"when\": \"The employee sends `GET /api/parking/claims/today`.\"\n },\n {\n  \"req\": \"REQ-13\",\n  \"given\": \"The employee has no temporary allocation for today or the request has no valid bearer token.\",\n  \"id\": \"AC-13.2\",\n  \"level\": \"api\",\n  \"then\": \"The response status is 404 or 401 respectively, and the response error contains the contract-defined `code`, `message`, and `field` values when an error response is returned.\",\n  \"when\": \"A client sends `GET /api/parking/claims/today`.\"\n },\n {\n  \"req\": \"REQ-14\",\n  \"given\": \"The bearer session owns an existing claim that can be cancelled.\",\n  \"id\": \"AC-14.1\",\n  \"level\": \"api\",\n  \"then\": \"The response status is 200 and the response contains the contract's `ParkingClaim` fields, including `id` and the cancellation outcome status.\",\n  \"when\": \"The employee deletes `/api/parking/claims/{claimId}`.\"\n },\n {\n  \"req\": \"REQ-14\",\n  \"given\": \"The claim does not exist, belongs to another employee, cannot be cancelled in its current state, or the request is unauthenticated.\",\n  \"id\": \"AC-14.2\",\n  \"level\": \"api\",\n  \"then\": \"The response status is 404, 403, 409, or 401 as applicable, and the response error contains the contract-defined `code`, `message`, and `field` values.\",\n  \"when\": \"A client deletes `/api/parking/claims/{claimId}`.\"\n },\n {\n  \"req\": \"REQ-15\",\n  \"given\": \"A valid administrator bearer session and optional `search`, `assignment`, `page`, and `pageSize` filters are supplied.\",\n  \"id\": \"AC-15.1\",\n  \"level\": \"api\",\n  \"then\": \"The response status is 200 and the response roster page contains `id`, `page`, `pages`, and an `employees` list with contract roster fields matching the supplied filters.\",\n  \"when\": \"The administrator sends `GET /api/admin/roster`.\"\n },\n {\n  \"req\": \"REQ-15\",\n  \"given\": \"The request is unauthenticated or the bearer token identifies a non-administrator.\",\n  \"id\": \"AC-15.2\",\n  \"level\": \"api\",\n  \"then\": \"The response status is 401 or 403 respectively, and the response error contains the contract-defined `code`, `message`, and `field` values.\",\n  \"when\": \"A client sends `GET /api/admin/roster`.\"\n },\n {\n  \"req\": \"REQ-16\",\n  \"given\": \"A valid administrator bearer session and optional `search`, `result`, and `page` filters are supplied.\",\n  \"id\": \"AC-16.1\",\n  \"level\": \"api\",\n  \"then\": \"The response status is 200 and the response page contains `id`, `page`, `pages`, and a `checks` list with contract entry-check fields matching the supplied filters.\",\n  \"when\": \"The administrator sends `GET /api/admin/entry-checks`.\"\n },\n {\n  \"req\": \"REQ-16\",\n  \"given\": \"The request is unauthenticated or the bearer token identifies a non-administrator.\",\n  \"id\": \"AC-16.2\",\n  \"level\": \"api\",\n  \"then\": \"The response status is 401 or 403 respectively, and the response error contains the contract-defined `code`, `message`, and `field` values.\",\n  \"when\": \"A client sends `GET /api/admin/entry-checks`.\"\n },\n {\n  \"req\": \"REQ-17\",\n  \"given\": \"A car detection has a readable plate with active temporary parking authorization for the detected office date.\",\n  \"id\": \"AC-17.1\",\n  \"level\": \"api\",\n  \"then\": \"The response status is 200 and the response reports the detected plate, `verificationResult` `Authorized`, `entryStatus`, and `indicatorCommand` `Green`.\",\n  \"when\": \"The client posts the detection to `/api/entrance/verify`.\"\n },\n {\n  \"req\": \"REQ-17\",\n  \"given\": \"The detection is a pedestrian, motorcycle, or other non-car object.\",\n  \"id\": \"AC-17.2\",\n  \"level\": \"api\",\n  \"then\": \"The response status is 200 and the response has a null `plate`, `indicatorCommand` `None`, and the contract-defined non-car outcome fields.\",\n  \"when\": \"The client posts the detection to `/api/entrance/verify`.\"\n },\n {\n  \"req\": \"REQ-17\",\n  \"given\": \"A car has no valid authorization, its plate is unreadable, or a required entrance service is unavailable.\",\n  \"id\": \"AC-17.3\",\n  \"level\": \"api\",\n  \"then\": \"The response reports a denied or unsuccessful outcome with `indicatorCommand` `None`, and the response status is 200 for processed detections or 503 for the unavailable-service outcome.\",\n  \"when\": \"The client posts the detection to `/api/entrance/verify`.\"\n },\n {\n  \"req\": \"REQ-17\",\n  \"given\": \"A detection has been processed, including a non-car or unsuccessful detection.\",\n  \"id\": \"AC-17.4\",\n  \"level\": \"api\",\n  \"then\": \"A database row records the detection time, office date and time, plate where available, verification result, entry status, and detail, and the response `checks` list contains the corresponding record.\",\n  \"when\": \"The client posts the detection and an administrator later requests matching entry checks.\"\n },\n {\n  \"req\": \"REQ-17\",\n  \"given\": \"An entrance detection request is malformed.\",\n  \"id\": \"AC-17.5\",\n  \"level\": \"api\",\n  \"then\": \"The response status is 400 and the response error contains the contract-defined `code`, `message`, and `field` values.\",\n  \"when\": \"A client posts to `/api/entrance/verify`.\"\n },\n {\n  \"req\": \"REQ-18\",\n  \"given\": \"A valid administrator bearer session and an omitted or valid `weekStart` date are supplied and parking activity exists for the requested week.\",\n  \"id\": \"AC-18.1\",\n  \"level\": \"api\",\n  \"then\": \"The response status is 200 and the response report contains `weekStart`, `weekEnd`, `generatedAt`, `releasedSpaces`, `temporaryClaims`, `overallUtilizationPercent`, `dailyStatistics`, and `unusedParking`.\",\n  \"when\": \"The administrator sends `GET /api/admin/utilization`.\"\n },\n {\n  \"req\": \"REQ-18\",\n  \"given\": \"The request is unauthenticated, the caller is not an administrator, or `weekStart` is invalid.\",\n  \"id\": \"AC-18.2\",\n  \"level\": \"api\",\n  \"then\": \"The response status is 401, 403, or 400 as applicable, and the response error contains the contract-defined `code`, `message`, and `field` values.\",\n  \"when\": \"A client sends `GET /api/admin/utilization`.\"\n },\n {\n  \"req\": \"REQ-19\",\n  \"given\": \"A valid administrator bearer session exists and office parking settings are stored in App.\",\n  \"id\": \"AC-19.1\",\n  \"level\": \"api\",\n  \"then\": \"The response status is 200 and the response contains `timezone`, `releaseTime`, `schedulingWindowDays`, `reportRecipients`, `nextReportDelivery`, and `reportSchedule` matching the stored settings.\",\n  \"when\": \"The administrator sends `GET /api/admin/office-settings`.\"\n },\n {\n  \"req\": \"REQ-19\",\n  \"given\": \"The request is unauthenticated or the bearer token identifies a non-administrator.\",\n  \"id\": \"AC-19.2\",\n  \"level\": \"api\",\n  \"then\": \"The response status is 401 or 403 respectively, and the response error contains the contract-defined `code`, `message`, and `field` values.\",\n  \"when\": \"A client sends `GET /api/admin/office-settings`.\"\n },\n {\n  \"req\": \"REQ-20\",\n  \"given\": \"A valid administrator bearer session and valid `timezone`, `releaseTime`, and non-empty `reportRecipients` are supplied.\",\n  \"id\": \"AC-20.1\",\n  \"level\": \"api\",\n  \"then\": \"The response status is 200 and the response contains the saved settings fields; a subsequent response from `GET /api/admin/office-settings` returns the saved values.\",\n  \"when\": \"The administrator updates `/api/admin/office-settings`.\"\n },\n {\n  \"req\": \"REQ-20\",\n  \"given\": \"The update is invalid, unauthenticated, or sent by a non-administrator.\",\n  \"id\": \"AC-20.2\",\n  \"level\": \"api\",\n  \"then\": \"The response status is 400, 401, or 403 as applicable, and the response error contains the contract-defined `code`, `message`, and `field` values.\",\n  \"when\": \"A client sends `PUT /api/admin/office-settings`.\"\n },\n {\n  \"req\": \"REQ-21\",\n  \"given\": \"A valid administrator bearer session and optional `search`, `eventType`, and `page` filters are supplied, and retained activity exists.\",\n  \"id\": \"AC-21.1\",\n  \"level\": \"api\",\n  \"then\": \"The response status is 200 and the response contains `page`, `pages`, and an `activity` list containing matching records with the contract activity fields.\",\n  \"when\": \"The administrator sends `GET /api/admin/activity`.\"\n },\n {\n  \"req\": \"REQ-21\",\n  \"given\": \"The request is unauthenticated or the bearer token identifies a non-administrator.\",\n  \"id\": \"AC-21.2\",\n  \"level\": \"api\",\n  \"then\": \"The response status is 401 or 403 respectively, and the response error contains the contract-defined `code`, `message`, and `field` values.\",\n  \"when\": \"A client sends `GET /api/admin/activity`.\"\n },\n {\n  \"req\": \"REQ-22\",\n  \"given\": \"A valid administrator bearer session and optional `search`, `eventType`, and `page` filters are supplied, and retained activity exists.\",\n  \"id\": \"AC-22.1\",\n  \"level\": \"api\",\n  \"then\": \"The response status is 200 and the response contains `id`, `page`, `pages`, and an `events` list containing matching records with the contract `ParkingActivity` fields.\",\n  \"when\": \"The administrator sends `GET /api/admin/activity`.\"\n },\n {\n  \"req\": \"REQ-22\",\n  \"given\": \"The request is unauthenticated or the bearer token identifies a non-administrator.\",\n  \"id\": \"AC-22.2\",\n  \"level\": \"api\",\n  \"then\": \"The response status is 401 or 403 respectively, and the response error contains the contract-defined `code`, `message`, and `field` values.\",\n  \"when\": \"A client sends `GET /api/admin/activity`.\"\n },\n {\n  \"req\": \"REQ-23\",\n  \"given\": \"A valid availability request has a positive `availableSpaces` value and the email service accepts dispatch for eligible non-dedicated employees.\",\n  \"id\": \"AC-23.1\",\n  \"level\": \"api\",\n  \"then\": \"The response status is 202 and the response dispatch contains request `id`, status `accepted`, `recipientCount`, and template `parking-availability`; an outbound call is recorded to the configured email delivery service for eligible recipients.\",\n  \"when\": \"The client posts to `/api/notifications/availability`.\"\n },\n {\n  \"req\": \"REQ-23\",\n  \"given\": \"The availability request is invalid or the required email service is unavailable.\",\n  \"id\": \"AC-23.2\",\n  \"level\": \"api\",\n  \"then\": \"The response status is 400 or 503 respectively, and the response error contains the contract-defined `code`, `message`, and `field` values.\",\n  \"when\": \"A client posts to `/api/notifications/availability`.\"\n },\n {\n  \"req\": \"REQ-24\",\n  \"given\": \"`ConnectionStrings:App` points to a fresh PostgreSQL database.\",\n  \"id\": \"AC-24.1\",\n  \"level\": \"api\",\n  \"then\": \"A row in PostgreSQL `information_schema.tables` identifies each created application table.\",\n  \"when\": \"The API starts.\"\n },\n {\n  \"req\": \"REQ-24\",\n  \"given\": \"A fresh App database is configured and demo seeding is disabled.\",\n  \"id\": \"AC-24.2\",\n  \"level\": \"api\",\n  \"then\": \"The registration response status is 201, a corresponding row exists in the configured App database, and the later response `vehicles` list contains the saved record.\",\n  \"when\": \"An authenticated client registers a vehicle, the API restarts against the same database, and the employee lists vehicles.\"\n },\n {\n  \"req\": \"REQ-25\",\n  \"given\": \"The App database schema exists, its application tables are empty, and `Seed:Demo` is true.\",\n  \"id\": \"AC-25.1\",\n  \"level\": \"api\",\n  \"then\": \"The row count is between two and five in every application table; each table has at least two schema-valid sample rows, including at least two in non-singleton tables and at least one valid row in any contract-defined singleton table, with contract examples where available such as Aisha Rahman's employee and Toyota Corolla vehicle.\",\n  \"when\": \"The API starts and invokes the public `SeedData.Run` method.\"\n },\n {\n  \"req\": \"REQ-25\",\n  \"given\": \"An empty database has its application tables created.\",\n  \"id\": \"AC-25.2\",\n  \"level\": \"unit\",\n  \"then\": \"Rows are present in each application table and each seeded row is schema-valid.\",